<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alhflæd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 650s</span> · Also known as Alhflaed</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alhflæd was a daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a> who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peada">Peada</a>, ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-angles">Middle Angles</a>, around 653, on condition that he accept baptism. The marriage brought Northumbrian missionaries into Mercian lands. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> reports that Peada was murdered in 656, betrayed, it was said, by his wife.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhflaed.jpg" alt="Alhflæd" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peada_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
